  "body": "Enables the mandated .githooks pre-push gate on Windows writer environments. No gate logic is weakened; every check still runs unchanged on Linux CI.\n\n- Resolve script-relative paths with fileURLToPath instead of URL.pathname, which yields /C:/... and breaks every git spawn on Windows (validate-intake.mjs, promote-intake.mjs, two tests, one generator \u2014 the same fix generate-index.mjs and the Dawncaster sidecar generator already carry).\n- Force lossy VP8 in webp test fixtures: ffmpeg 8 auto-selects lossless VP8X for flat lavfi sources, and ffmpeg's native webp decoder cannot read those back when assembling the contact sheet.\n- fail-closed: Windows-spawnable .cmd hermes shim in the test (redirect-first so job ids cannot form fd-redirects), USERPROFILE set alongside HOME, and shell:true on win32 only in the production spawn (POSIX behavior identical).\n- Probe symlink capability once per test file and skip the two symlink-escape tests where creation is denied (Windows without Developer Mode). Linux CI always exercises both.\n\nFound while pushing a docs-only branch: this machine had never set core.hooksPath, so this was the first local run of the gate.\n\nGenerated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
